{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01Gm2R7pu2ErKki4kJYC5umx","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The file has been written! Here's a summary of what's in the ~7,200-word document at `/Users/sarthakagarwal/Desktop/projects/prep/system-design/payments-system/answers/03-state-management-transaction-lifecycle.md`:\n\n---\n\n**## Core (7 answers)**\n\n| # | Topic | Key content |\n|---|-------|-------------|\n| Q1 | PaymentIntent FSM → UI rendering | `stateDiagram-v2` of all PI states, React `switch`-based render dispatcher, `handleNextAction()` for 3DS, polling for `processing` |\n| Q2 | Idempotency & safe retries | `getOrCreateIdempotencyKey()` with `crypto.randomUUID()` + `sessionStorage`, `Idempotency-Key` header, PaymentIntent as natural idempotency boundary |\n| Q3 | Optimistic UI limits | Hybrid by risk — optimistic for cart mutations, pessimistic-with-spinner for actual charge, rollback strategy |\n| Q4 | State persistence across refresh | 3-tier model (URL params / sessionStorage / server session), `rehydrateCheckoutState()`, what to **never** persist (PAN, CVV, `client_secret` in localStorage) |\n| Q5 | Tab close during `processing` | `handleReEntry()` with full recovery paths per status, exponential-backoff polling loop |\n| Q6 | Concurrent tab conflicts | `BroadcastChannel` API with `CART_UPDATED` / `PAYMENT_INITIATED` events, optimistic locking + 409 Conflict handling |\n| Q7 | Ad blocker strips redirect params | `resolvePaymentStatus()` with layered fallback (URL params → server poll → `stripe.retrievePaymentIntent()`), resolution flowchart |\n\n**## Deep (3 answers)**\n\n| # | Topic | Key content |\n|---|-------|-------------|\n| D1 | Soft-decline retry loop | `RETRY_CONFIG` with soft/hard decline code sets, full `attemptPayment()` loop with state transitions diagram |\n| D2 | XState payment machine | Complete v4 `createMachine` with 8 states (`idle`, `submitting`, `requiresAction`, `processing`, `softDeclined`, `networkError`, `hardDeclined`, `succeeded`), guards/actions/services, `useMachine` React integration |\n| D3 | WebView postMessage bridge | Unified iOS/Android bridge abstraction, ACK protocol with exponential backoff, 5 failure modes + mitigations, Swift `WKScriptMessageHandler` pseudocode, architecture flowchart |"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a5d9fbf65b4573271 (use SendMessage with to: 'a5d9fbf65b4573271' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 24410\ntool_uses: 1\nduration_ms: 733275</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b5e4a3c-6477-40c1-bb5a-cf9fbc849288","uuid":"9a16b694-656e-48e6-8eb1-574214a0430f","timestamp":"2026-06-20T18:57:16.353Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Write a comprehensive answers file for the payments-system system design topic, section 03: State Management & Transaction Lifecycle.\n\nOutput file: `/Users/sarthakagarwal/Desktop/projects/prep/system-design/payments-system/answers/03-state-management-transaction-lifecycle.md`\n\n## Section questions to answer\n\n### Core questions:\n1. A Stripe `PaymentIntent` moves through states: `requires_payment_method` → `requires_confirmation` → `requires_action` → `processing` → `succeeded` (or `requires_capture`, `canceled`). How does your frontend model this state machine, and how do you decide which UI to render at each transition?\n2. What is idempotency in the context of payment requests, and how do you implement it on the frontend? Specifically, if a user clicks \"Pay\" and the request times out before you receive a response, how do you safely retry without charging the user twice?\n3. How do you handle optimistic UI in a payment flow? Unlike a social media \"like,\" a payment has real monetary consequence if the optimistic update is wrong. Where do you draw the line between responsiveness and correctness?\n4. Describe how you would manage the state of a multi-step checkout form across a full page refresh. What should be persisted (to `sessionStorage`, a URL param, or a server-side cart session), and what should be intentionally discarded to avoid security issues?\n5. What happens to an in-flight payment confirmation if the user's browser tab is closed or the device loses power during the `processing` state? How does your frontend handle re-entry — e.g., the user re-opens the tab or returns to the site 10 minutes later?\n6. How do you handle concurrent modifications to a shared cart — e.g., the same user opens checkout in two browser tabs simultaneously? How do you detect the conflict on the frontend and recover gracefully?\n7. A user completes payment but the success redirect is intercepted by an ad blocker or a browser extension that strips query params. How do you design the confirmation flow so the user reaches a correct success state even if your `?payment_intent=pi_xxx&redirect_status=succeeded` URL param never arrives?\n\n### Deep questions:\n1. Walk me through implementing a robust payment retry loop on the frontend. The user's card was declined (soft decline). You want to: (1) allow the user to update their card details, (2) re-confirm the same `PaymentIntent` rather than creating a new one, and (3) cap retries at a safe limit to avoid locking the card. How do you manage the state transitions, and what data do you pass back to the `confirmCardPayment` call on a retry?\n2. Describe how you would architect a frontend payment state machine using XState (or a comparable library). Define the states, events, guards, and side effects for the full lifecycle including 3DS authentication, network errors, and soft declines. What are the advantages of this approach over ad-hoc `if/else` logic in React component state?\n3. Your checkout frontend runs inside a mobile WebView embedded in a native iOS/Android app. The native app and the WebView both need to know the payment outcome. Walk through the communication architecture: how does a payment confirmation event travel from the Stripe SDK (inside the WebView) through the `postMessage` bridge to the native layer, what are the failure modes, and how do you ensure exactly-once delivery of the success event to the native app?\n\n## Answer format (REQUIRED for every question)\nEach answer must have exactly these three sections:\n1. **Problem framing:** restate the question and why it matters\n2. **Approach:** your solution with mechanisms, code snippets, and Mermaid diagrams where helpful\n3. **Tradeoffs:** alternatives considered and why you chose this path\n\n## File format\n\nThe file should be a markdown file with:\n- `# Section 3: State Management & Transaction Lifecycle` heading\n- A brief intro paragraph\n- `## Core` heading with all 7 core answers\n- `## Deep` heading with all 3 deep answers\n- Each question as `### Q: <question text>` followed by the three-part answer\n\nFor Mermaid diagrams (in Approach sections), use:\n```mermaid\nstateDiagram-v2\n  ...\n```\n\n## Quality bar\n- Answers should be interview-depth: concrete, specific, technically accurate\n- Include specific Stripe API details (PaymentIntent states, error codes, etc.)\n- Include code snippets for key mechanisms (idempotency key generation, XState machine definition, postMessage bridge)\n- Cover edge cases (network timeout vs definitive failure, ad blocker stripping params, etc.)\n- The XState question should show actual machine config with states, events, guards, actions\n- The retry loop question should show actual state transitions and data flow\n- Target ~400-600 words per answer for Core questions, ~600-900 words for Deep questions\n\nWrite the full file now.","agentId":"a5d9fbf65b4573271","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The file has been written! Here's a summary of what's in the ~7,200-word document at `/Users/sarthakagarwal/Desktop/projects/prep/system-design/payments-system/answers/03-state-management-transaction-lifecycle.md`:\n\n---\n\n**## Core (7 answers)**\n\n| # | Topic | Key content |\n|---|-------|-------------|\n| Q1 | PaymentIntent FSM → UI rendering | `stateDiagram-v2` of all PI states, React `switch`-based render dispatcher, `handleNextAction()` for 3DS, polling for `processing` |\n| Q2 | Idempotency & safe retries | `getOrCreateIdempotencyKey()` with `crypto.randomUUID()` + `sessionStorage`, `Idempotency-Key` header, PaymentIntent as natural idempotency boundary |\n| Q3 | Optimistic UI limits | Hybrid by risk — optimistic for cart mutations, pessimistic-with-spinner for actual charge, rollback strategy |\n| Q4 | State persistence across refresh | 3-tier model (URL params / sessionStorage / server session), `rehydrateCheckoutState()`, what to **never** persist (PAN, CVV, `client_secret` in localStorage) |\n| Q5 | Tab close during `processing` | `handleReEntry()` with full recovery paths per status, exponential-backoff polling loop |\n| Q6 | Concurrent tab conflicts | `BroadcastChannel` API with `CART_UPDATED` / `PAYMENT_INITIATED` events, optimistic locking + 409 Conflict handling |\n| Q7 | Ad blocker strips redirect params | `resolvePaymentStatus()` with layered fallback (URL params → server poll → `stripe.retrievePaymentIntent()`), resolution flowchart |\n\n**## Deep (3 answers)**\n\n| # | Topic | Key content |\n|---|-------|-------------|\n| D1 | Soft-decline retry loop | `RETRY_CONFIG` with soft/hard decline code sets, full `attemptPayment()` loop with state transitions diagram |\n| D2 | XState payment machine | Complete v4 `createMachine` with 8 states (`idle`, `submitting`, `requiresAction`, `processing`, `softDeclined`, `networkError`, `hardDeclined`, `succeeded`), guards/actions/services, `useMachine` React integration |\n| D3 | WebView postMessage bridge | Unified iOS/Android bridge abstraction, ACK protocol with exponential backoff, 5 failure modes + mitigations, Swift `WKScriptMessageHandler` pseudocode, architecture flowchart |"}],"resolvedModel":"blackboxai/anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.5","totalDurationMs":733275,"totalTokens":24410,"tot